From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zram: default to lz4

Android 17 leaves the zram compressor at the kernel default (mmd only
configures recompression), which on 4.19 is lzo-rle, and lz4 was not
even selectable because CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4 was off. Enable it and make
lz4 the default compressor when it is built in: decompression, which is
what returning to a swapped-out app waits on, is considerably faster
than lzo-rle at a similar ratio. lzo-rle stays the default otherwise and
remains selectable through comp_algorithm.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
@@ -6342,7 +6342,7 @@
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEFLATE=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZO=y
 # CONFIG_CRYPTO_842 is not set
-# CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4 is not set
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4=y
 # CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4HC is not set
 # CONFIG_CRYPTO_ZSTD is not set
 
diff --git a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
--- a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
@@ -54,7 +54,15 @@
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(zram_index_mutex);
 
 static int zram_major;
+/*
+ * lz4 decompresses considerably faster than lzo-rle on the Cortex-A77/A55
+ * with a similar ratio, which shortens swap-in when returning to cached apps.
+ */
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4)
+static const char *default_compressor = "lz4";
+#else
 static const char *default_compressor = "lzo-rle";
+#endif
 
 /* Module params (documentation at end) */
 static unsigned int num_devices = 1;
